     Inews(8L)             OS-9 (News)             Inews(8L)     NNAAMMEE                  Inews - NetNews Management System      SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS                  inews [-v] [-a] [-g=<grplist>] [-d=<distlist>] [-t] [-D]               [-e=<days>] [-E=<days>] [-r]               [-h] [-R]               [-c=<ctrlmsg>:<ctrl-opts>]               [-M=<msgid>]     DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN                     Inews is   the  program  which  does  the  whole         management  on the local news system. In normal use         it  is  started  without  any option and parses the         header,   then  write  the  article  in  the  right         directory  matching the given newsgroups. A special         kind  of a message is the control message (refer to         RFC1036)    where   only   a   few   are   executed         immediately,   other   are   mailed   to  the  news         administrator.  To  execute these you have to start         inews  with  the option --aa to switch to admin mode.         An explaination of the options follows.                --aa Runs  inews  in  admin  mode to execute all                fed   control   messages.   This  option  is                obsolete,  to  enter  admin mode you have to                be user news or superuser.                --ee==<<ddaayyss>> Starts  to  delete all article which                have  been  arrived  here  more  than <days>                ago.  If  a  list  of  groups is given, only                these groups are affected.                --EE==<<ddaayyss>> This  option  is used in combination                with  `-e'.   While  `-e'  give  the time to                expire  old articles, `-E' gives the time to                delete  the  Message-ID:  from  the  history                database.    It   is   useful   to   keep  a                historyfile  as  large  as possible to avoid     Page 1                            