       --MM==<<mmssggiidd>> If  an  external  process  wants to                retreive  an article with a given message id                and  doesn't  know which filename belongs to                this  id  he can call inews with this option                and  the required message id. If he wants to                retreive  more  than one, this option can be                given  as  often as desired. The output will                be either                        +<message-id> <TAB> <filename>                                     or                               -<message-id>                where  the  first  line  will be written, if                the  message  id  was  found,  otherwise the                other   line  will  be  the  format  of  the                output.       CCAAVVEEAATTSS                     Inews isn't  a  complete  newssystem, but just a         working  subset.  It  is  tested against BNews 2.11         and  seems  to  work okay. It won't work with older         ANews versions.       BBUUGGSS                     Maybe a  lot.  But none known. It runs just fine         for years on several systems until now.       FFIILLEESS                    //hh00//SSPPOOOOLL//NNEEWWSS Here  in  all  articles are placed             in subdirectories.             //hh00//UUSSRR//LLIIBB//NNEEWWSS All   configuration   files  are             placed here, these are:                AAccttiivvee The active list of newsgroups.       Page 3                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)     Inews(8L)             OS-9 (News)             Inews(8L)               AAlliiaasseess A list of aliases for newsgroups.                 AArrcchhiivvee If   articles  of  a  specific  group                 shouldn't  be  deleted  but archived during                 an   expire  this  files  contains  details                 which  groups  are  affected  and  where to                 store them.                 CChheecckkggrroouuppss A   kist   to  limit  checkgroups                 depending on the distribution.                 CCoonnvvttaabbllee If  you  forward  news  to a system                 which  only  supports  7  bit character and                 you  use locally 8 bit character this files                 descripes  how  to  map  these  characters.                 This  file  can also map 7 bit to 7 bit (if                 you  want to change something, e.g. replace                 every tab by two spaces.)                DDiissttrriibbuuttiioonnss The  default  distributions for                 several newsgroups.                 FFoolllloowwuupp This  describes default followups to                 some   newsgroups,   e.g.   a  followup  in                 alt.sources    should    be    placed    in                 alt.sources.d.                 LLooggffiillee The   logfile   of   news;   if   not                 existing, it isn't written.                 SSyyss The systems to feed news to.                 sseenndd__uuuunnaammee The   file   to  be  send  on  an                 senduuname control message.             //hh00//UUSSRR//LLIIBB//NNEEWWSS//HHIISSTTOORRYY      Page 4                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)     Inews(8L)             OS-9 (News)             Inews(8L)           //hh00//UUSSRR//LLIIBB//NNEEWWSS//HHiissttoorryyDDBBMM..((ddiirr||ppaagg))         All             arrived   article   IDs  to  prevent  duplicate             articles  (the  2nd format is valid, if you are             using ndbm.)      SSYYSSIINNFFOO                      MNEWS.BATCH,s=/h0/SPOOL/BATCH             MNEWS.DIR,s=/h0/SPOOL/NEWS             MNEWS.LIB,s=/h0/USR/LIB/NEWS             lck.inews,l             hostname,s=<